    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Bryce Harper** (78.76) as our absolute anchor; he draws a favorable matchup against Alcantara, where his elite 0.390 xwOBA and strong BvP history (60 PA) elevate his ceiling significantly, making him the cornerstone of our lineup. **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) is our second-strongest play, benefiting from a robust 13% platoon edge against Lugo and high-leverage spot in the four-hole. We are also leaning into **Jonathan Aranda** (67.95) today; while the base projection was modest, a 5.08 xERA from Scherzer and a massive 19% boost for SP weakness make him an undervalued asset, particularly as he occupies the #3 spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Masyn Winn** (46.70), who sat right on the fringe of a viable start. Ultimately, he was relegated to the bench because the matchup against Burns (3.50 xERA) presented too much volatility; the optimizer favored the efficiency of **Brendan Donovan** and **Luis Arraez** to protect our 5x5 categories. Similarly, **Gleyber Torres** fell below our 40.0 floor, yielding his spot as his projections cratered against Skenes\u2019 elite arm. We are monitoring **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** closely; his raw talent is undeniable, but a 0.00 xERA matchup against Wilkinson essentially neutralizes his upside, dragging his efficiency score down to 57.32.\n\nRisk management remains a priority today, as our C1 **Cal Raleigh** (51.35) is facing May, an arm that limits his effectiveness, compounded by a bottom-third batting order position. We are keeping a close eye on **JJ Bleday** (60.49), whose score is buoyed heavily by a 14% platoon edge against Liberatore; if the winds at the stadium shift, his floor could collapse quickly. Ensure game caps are monitored closely, as players like **Braden Montgomery** (47.63) provide only marginal utility today and should be treated as the first candidates to pull if we are approaching our total inning or game caps.",
